    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d141">

                <pb facs="0195" n="123" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg123"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 5767/142.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador O’Brien to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1909-12-08"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">December 8, 1909</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 901.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: On November 13th I had the honor to
                    transmit with my dispatch No, 863<anchor n="2" xml:id="d141-f1"/> a copy of my
                    note to the minister for foreign affairs <pb facs="0196" n="124" xml:id="pg124"
                    /> of the same date, touching the agreements of September 4 between Japan and
                    China. I now beg to inclose a copy of his reply, dated November 25.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. J. O’Brien.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d141-a1.xml" xpointer="d141-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
